<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian Thomasius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1655">1655</a>–<a href="/years/1728">1728</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian Thomasius (1655–1728) was a German jurist and philosopher, one of the founders of the early German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a>. Forced out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> for his views, he moved to Halle in 1690 and helped found its university. He lectured in German rather than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, separated law from theology and campaigned against witch trials and torture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-thomasius.jpg" alt="Christian Thomasius" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Christian Heinrich Sporleder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_Thomasius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
